            <ArticleTitle>New therapeutic perspectives in non-alcoholic steatohepatitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0210-5705(17)30183-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.gastrohep.2017.07.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Management of non-alcoholic steatohepatitis is focused on restitution of metabolic derangement, weight loss and drugs able to improve steatosis, ballooning and fibrosis. Life-style interventions based on Mediterranean diet and increasing physical activity are the first line therapy. In patients with unsuccessful life-style intervention several drugs are under development: agonist PPAR, agonist GLP-1R and agonist FXR together with drugs focussing on inflammation, ballooning, apoptosis and fibrosis. Bariatric surgery or advanced endoscopy are reserved for morbid obese without response to life-style intervention and weighting loss drugs.</AbstractText>
